\citation{yin2016synthesis}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The DFAs $G_1$ and $G_2$ are shown in subfigures~(a) and~(b), respectively, with observable event set $\Sigma _o = \{ o_1, o_2, o_3, o_4\}$ and marked-state set $Q_m = \{ q_5 \}$. The shaded regions represent identical observation-induced state estimates, and the corresponding estimate transitions are the same in both systems, showing that $G_1$ and $G_2$ induce the same observer-level structure. $G_1$ is blocking because $q_1$ and $q_3$ are not co-accessible to $q_5$, whereas $G_2$ is non-blocking owing to its cross-coupled transitions.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
