\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Inter-connected bipartite transition system constructed from the DFA $G$ in Fig.~\ref {fig:dfa_grid_env} (b). We simplify the notations $(\hat  {q}, \hat  {x})$ and $(q, x, \gamma )$ to $\hat  {q}$ and $q$, respectively, and omit the uncontrollable events contained in each control pattern to better illustrate the structural properties of each state. Orange rectangles represent decision macrostates, while blue rounded rectangles represent observation macrostates. Transitions in different colors are used to distinguish different evolutions. Moreover, the information states marked by red crosses are infeasible observation macrostates, detectably blocking decision macrostates, or inconsistent decision or observation macrostates, which should be pruned to achieve detectable non-blocking. The source code is available at \url {https://github.com/trigger1996/des_common/tree/master/detectable_nonblocking}.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
