\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Conceptual illustration of the correspondence between detectable non-blockingness and the structural properties of IC-BTS. A run of the IC-BTS captures the evolution of the controlled DES at both the observation level and the DFA-state level. A detectably non-blocking execution requires that every reachable state admits a path to a detectably marked decision state, where observation states along the path are potentially feasible, and decision states are detectably live. Conversely, any IC-BTS representing a detectably non-blocking closed-loop system must preserve these properties and satisfy observation consistency. The red-crossed components indicate branches violating potential feasibility, detectable liveness, or consistency, which cannot appear in a valid detectably non-blocking IC-BTS.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:conceptual_proof}{{5}{11}{}{figure.5}{}}
